# The native Android project. It is a full Gradle workspace (wrapper, plugin
# sources, build outputs) that the server image has no use for, and without this
# it would be copied into the builder stage on every build — inflating the build
# context and invalidating the user-panel source layer whenever a native file
# changes. The APK is built by .github/workflows/android-release.yml, not here.
user-panel/android

# Build-context weight with no runtime consumer: the unbuilt screen sketch, the
# governance corpus, audit archives and dev tooling. None of it is COPYed into
# any stage; excluding it keeps the context small so `docker build` starts fast.
design
docs
audit
tools
platform
deploy
